WI-kikar: Node's `process` and `performance` are runtime globals, so their member
calls carry a module slot instead of the `external` sentinel.

THE GAP. `process.on('message', h)` and `process.send(x)` resolved to
`javascript:external:0-0:on:unresolved` while `console.log`,
`localStorage.setItem` and `navigator.sendBeacon` — member calls on other named
globals — resolved with their slot filled. `process` was missing from
`JS_KNOWN_GLOBALS`, the set the Case-3b member-call fallback consults for a
receiver that needs no import. `external` is ADR-0051's marker for *unreachable
to the catalogue*: a false negative by construction.

THE FILING NAMED TWO ROWS. THE PROBE FOUND EIGHT CALLS ACROSS TWO GLOBALS.
The break is in the member-call path, not the row kind, so the FUNCTION-kind
rows on `process` broke identically — `hrtime`, `uptime`, `getuid`,
`memoryUsage`, `chdir`, `openStdin` (33 rows in all, across ipc_recv, ipc_send,
host_info_read, env_write, fs_read). And `performance.now()` is a SECOND global
with the same shape, absent from the filing entirely. Enumerating every
method/function-kind module in `javascript.yaml` against its resolution route
found exactly these two with no route at all.

